{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact OAuth design head 73946d0f90be46c534c3b021c394357a47f593ca on planner/mcp-oauth-design-20261102-r2, notes/2026-11-02-hosted-mcp-oauth.md, for request 3f598e55 under review request 1712cfbf. This approval covers the design only. A builder may take O1 and O2 now, and O3 after both.\n\nScope. Main bcf88654 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The only commit since 6abcdb43 changes the note's resource-server section, the grant example, the token audience and the O1 and O4 rows. The six points that passed in 4b4aca58 stand, and their cited lines still hold at bcf88654.\n\nPoint 7 is met. Each connector URL is now its own protected resource:\n\n- MCP_RESOURCE_URLS lists at most 8 canonical HTTPS URLs at /mcp, and every MCP_CARD_ORIGINS URL must appear in it. A card origin and a token audience therefore follow the same URL. An absent setting means https://\u003cservice\u003e/mcp alone, and an invalid one closes the endpoint.\n- The metadata route keeps the query and returns that exact URL as resource, as RFC 9728 sections 3.1 and 3.3 require. A query that matches no configured URL answers 404.\n- The 401 challenge carries the request's own query, so each host finds its own metadata.\n- The token route accepts resource only when it equals a configured URL, and the access check compares the audience with the exact request URL. That is the key remoteCardDomain already uses: the service origin plus the request's path and query.\n\nNo step widens authority. A mismatch between the token's audience and the request URL answers 401, so a token cannot cross from one connector URL to the other. Static bearers stay outside the audience check, as before. O1 now controls a token used at the other connector URL and an unmatched metadata query. O4 connects both hosts to one deployment at once and acts from each.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Security: no blocking finding. Simplification: no change needed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:70a3dbc5e0e5392daf614b06f6e3ba91a75151e2","binding":"assigned","head":"73946d0f90be46c534c3b021c394357a47f593ca","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea843aab003468dc994c056f670ff76e0b3915ca\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b104c840ec1ce4b352f3971136e6a036dc5b2c47\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea843aab003468dc994c056f670ff76e0b3915ca","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}